---
import MainLayout from '../../layouts/MainLayout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../components/SiteFooter.astro';
---
<MainLayout
  title="Operations Dashboard | Phillip Pieterse"
  description="Case study for an Operations Dashboard focused on live shipment visibility, exception tracking, and reporting truth."
>
  <SiteHeader />

  <main class="page-shell">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="page-head">
        <div class="eyebrow">Case study</div>
        <h1 class="page-title">Operations Dashboard</h1>
        <p class="page-copy">
          A live internal dashboard for shipment visibility, exception tracking, and operational decision support.
          Built to make fast-changing work clearer, easier to monitor, and easier to act on.
        </p>
      </div>

      <section class="surface case-study-hero">
        <div>
          <div class="badge-row">
            <span class="badge live">Flagship project</span>
            <span class="tag">Next.js</span>
            <span class="tag">TypeScript</span>
            <span class="tag">Prisma</span>
            <span class="tag">PostgreSQL</span>
          </div>

          <h2>Built for visibility, control, and intervention speed.</h2>
          <p class="detail-copy">
            The dashboard brings operational truth into one surface: live KPIs, exception queues, admin controls,
            reporting views, and monitoring tools that help teams move from raw data to action faster.
          </p>

          <div class="detail-grid">
            <article class="detail-card">
              <div class="detail-label">Role</div>
              <div class="detail-value">Frontend + logic + reporting</div>
            </article>
            <article class="detail-card">
              <div class="detail-label">Focus</div>
              <div class="detail-value">Clarity under pressure</div>
            </article>
            <article class="detail-card">
              <div class="detail-label">Outcome</div>
              <div class="detail-value">Faster follow-up</div>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="project-preview">
          <img src="/images/projects/operations-dashboard/live-overview.png" alt="Operations dashboard live overview screenshot" />
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <div class="section-head">
          <div class="eyebrow">What it delivers</div>
          <h2 class="section-title">Core strengths</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="highlight-grid">
          <article class="highlight-card">
            <h3>Live KPI monitoring</h3>
            <p class="detail-copy">
              Tracks the current state of the operation with immediate visibility into packages, delivery progress, and risk.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="highlight-card">
            <h3>Branch drilldowns</h3>
            <p class="detail-copy">
              Lets users move from the big picture into the branch or team level without losing context.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="highlight-card">
            <h3>Late-risk monitoring</h3>
            <p class="detail-copy">
              Surfaces likely problem areas early so action can happen before the operation falls behind.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="highlight-card">
            <h3>Admin control surfaces</h3>
            <p class="detail-copy">
              Adds practical tooling around workers, sync visibility, controls, and shared operational settings.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <div class="section-head">
          <div class="eyebrow">Screenshots</div>
          <h2 class="section-title">Inside the dashboard</h2>
          <p class="section-copy">
            These views show the system from both sides: operational monitoring for action, and control surfaces for management.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="screenshot-grid">
          <figure class="screenshot-card">
            <img src="/images/projects/operations-dashboard/live-overview.png" alt="Live overview KPI screenshot" />
            <figcaption>Live overview focused on current package state, pending work, and operational breakdowns.</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure class="screenshot-card">
            <img src="/images/projects/operations-dashboard/control-tower.png" alt="Control tower and dashboard views screenshot" />
            <figcaption>Control tower entry point with navigation into live views, reporting, exceptions, and admin spaces.</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure class="screenshot-card">
            <img src="/images/projects/operations-dashboard/admin-controls.png" alt="Admin controls screenshot" />
            <figcaption>Administrative control surfaces for operational truth, settings, and access to management tools.</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure class="screenshot-card">
            <img src="/images/projects/operations-dashboard/worker-center.png" alt="Worker center screenshot" />
            <figcaption>Worker center with scheduler controls, sync run status, timing, and operational health indicators.</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <div class="surface">
          <div class="section-head">
            <div class="eyebrow">Why it matters</div>
            <h2 class="section-title">This is the kind of work I enjoy most.</h2>
            <p class="section-copy">
              I like building systems that connect real operations to useful interfaces — not just something that looks good,
              but something that helps teams see the truth of the work, reduce noise, and make better decisions.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="primary-button" href="/projects">Back to projects</a>
            <a class="ghost-button" href="https://github.com/Sleek1598" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">GitHub profile</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>

  <SiteFooter />
</MainLayout>
